hw/usb/hcd-dwc2: a channel the guest halts keeps no pending packet

When a guest writes HCCHAR.CHDIS to stop a channel, the model sets
CHHLTD but leaves the channel's DWC2Packet with needs_service set.
dwc2_work_bh then services that stale packet on the next frame timer,
re-reading HCCHAR/HCTSIZ/HCDMA -- which by now describe whatever the
guest has programmed into the channel since -- and issues a USB
transaction the guest never asked for: a duplicate OUT packet, or an
IN that consumes a device's queued data into a buffer nobody is
waiting on.

Seen with a guest whose bulk IN reads time out and halt the channel
every 200 ms (Inferno's usbdwc.c on -M raspi3b) and -device usb-net:
the DHCP OFFER was read by a stale IN service and lost, and every
DISCOVER after the first was garbled inside usb-net's RNDIS
reassembly by a duplicated packet. Two boots in five got an address.

Clear needs_service on a disable, cancel an in-flight async packet,
and have the work loop service only channels that are still enabled.

--- a/hw/usb/hcd-dwc2.c
+++ b/hw/usb/hcd-dwc2.c
@@ -585,7 +585,7 @@
 
     do {
         p = &s->packet[chan];
-        if (p->needs_service) {
+        if (p->needs_service && (s->hreg1[chan * 8] & HCCHAR_CHENA)) {
             dev = dwc2_find_device(s, p->devadr);
             ep = usb_ep_get(dev, p->pid, p->epnum);
             trace_usb_dwc2_work_bh_service(s->next_chan, chan, dev, p->epnum);
@@ -1042,6 +1042,15 @@
     *mmio = val;
 
     if (disflg) {
+        DWC2Packet *p = &s->packet[index >> 3];
+
+        /* the channel is halted: nothing of its transfer is pending any more */
+        if (p->async == DWC2_ASYNC_INFLIGHT) {
+            usb_cancel_packet(&p->packet);
+            usb_packet_cleanup(&p->packet);
+            p->async = DWC2_ASYNC_NONE;
+        }
+        p->needs_service = false;
         /* set ChHltd in HCINT */
         s->hreg1[(index & ~7) + 2] |= HCINTMSK_CHHLTD;
         iflg = 1;
